# Bandit's Talent: "{B}: Level 2". On turn 1 both Moxen are tapped for the Class's {1}{B}, and with the stack empty
# again (two passes: the spell, then its enters trigger) Level 2 is refused: nothing is left to pay its {B}, and it is
# sorcery speed in Bot1's own main phase so only the cost can be what refuses it. On turn 3 the Moxen have untapped and the
# same activation, paid by Mox Jet, is the positive control: the Class becomes level 2, shown by Bot2 (one card in hand
# after the enters discard) losing 2 life at its turn-4 upkeep.

